            <ArticleTitle>Use of the Crossboss catheter in coronary chronic total occlusion due to in-stent restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E30-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.23188</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe treatment of six chronic total occlusions due to in-stent restenosis with the CrossBoss catheter (BridgePoint Medical, Minneapolis, Minnesota). The CrossBoss catheter allowed successful CTO crossing in 5 of 6 lesions (83%): in 50% the catheter entered the distal true lumen, whereas in 33% a wire was required for distal true lumen crossing. No complications were observed. Use of the CrossBoss catheter can facilitate treatment of coronary chronic total occlusions due to in-stent restenosis.</AbstractText>
